{"id": "biz-3", "headline": "Medicaid work rules add barriers after disasters", "source": "KFF Health News", "url": "https://kffhealthnews.org/medicaid/natural-disasters-medicaid-work-requirements-eligibility-barriers-hawaii/", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["A month after Hurricane Lowell hit Kauai, Hawaii, unemployment claims on the island jumped from 69 before the September storm to about 1,800 nearly two weeks later, with heavy layoffs in tourism. Medicaid applications from island residents rose about 50% the following month. But new work rules in the One Big Beautiful Bill Act put enrollees in disaster-hit counties at risk of losing coverage. The law requires many nondisabled adults in 43 states and Washington, D. C. , to work, volunteer or study at least 80 hours a month, with eligibility checks starting in January.", "In most states, disaster victims can get a short-term exemption, but advocates worry the paperwork will leave gaps when people need coverage most. Source: KFF Health News."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110011001001101101100001011101111111", "10000010100011111100110011011110001000001", "10111010010001000111011000011011101011101", "10111010111010111000101011111101001011101", "10111010010010010010010100001011101011101", "10000010100010011000111000110000101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000001110110010011010000000000000000", "11111011111101110100101001110101010101010", "01001101101000001011101101001101111111001", "00001110000010011010110000011010000000000", "00111101111010110000011010111000010111000", "00100011110010000010000011101101000101110", "01010101110001111000110101001011101111001", "01010111000110000001000000011100100001000", "00110000110100101001110100110001111101010", "10001110101111100101001011110100000000100", "01001101010111001101100100001101111110001", "10001010001001110100101010111000010100000", "10111001011111011111011100101010101001000", "1001011100110011100011010110010001